  "comment": "Column order of the three quest tables, from poe-tool-dev/dat-schema (PoE2 entries only). Offsets are NOT stored: they are arithmetic over the widths in DatColumns, and recomputing them is what keeps this honest when a width is corrected. Vendored rather than downloaded so the feature works offline and so a schema refresh is a visible diff. MEASURED AGAINST A REAL INSTALL (2026-08): QuestStates computes 208 and the file's rows ARE 208 over 1477 rows; QuestFlags computes 12 and the file agrees over 5717, which is also the 0x0C row stride the schema measured in memory - so two of the three are confirmed exactly. QUEST DOES NOT AGREE: the file is 119 bytes over 127 rows against the 103 computed here, so one 16-byte column has been added that this schema does not carry. It is still USED, because both of dat-schema's Quest variants agree on the first four columns - Id +0, Act +8, Name +12, Icon_DDSFile +20 - and the three fields read here are among them; the mismatch is settled by READING Id and Name across the table rather than by trusting either number. Do not 'fix' the column list by padding it: the extra column's position is unknown, and inventing one in the wrong place would move Name without anything noticing. MAPPINS ADDED 2026-08 for the 'where' half of a step: it carries no coordinates - Name, WorldArea and Act - so a pin answers WHICH PLACE rather than which point, which is what a world-map pin is. QuestStates reaches them through MapPinsKeys (an array) and MapPinsKey (a single), and both are read because a state may use either.",
